       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 100 mg is ten times the maximum recommended daily dose. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the ceiling. A single 100 mg dose could cause profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make that dose safe.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, which is a common starting or maintenance dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a lower starting dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 100 mg, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
