       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I understand you're the chair and you've confirmed it. But 100 mg of amlodipine once daily is a dose that could seriously harm this patient, and no indication I know of supports it. Confirming it doesn't change the risk, which is severe hypotension and shock that can last for days because amlodipine has a half-life of 30\u201350 hours.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **I can enter a standard dose right now.** That could be 10 mg, 5 mg, or 2.5 mg by mouth once daily. If the goal is stronger blood pressure control, I can also enter a second agent.\n- **If this is an unusual situation**, such as a dose carried over from a different formulation or a typo, tell me what the intended order is and I'll enter that.\n- **If you still want 100 mg**, that decision should go through pharmacy and a direct prescriber-to-pharmacist conversation. It shouldn't go through me.\n\nWhich would you like?"
